{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"611","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. New Year and Cleaning"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Limak is a little polar bear. His parents told him to clean a house before the New Year's Eve. Their house is a rectangular grid with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":" rows and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"w"},{"kind":"text","text":" columns. Each cell is an empty square."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"He is a little bear and thus he can't clean a house by himself. Instead, he is going to use a cleaning robot."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A cleaning robot has a built-in pattern of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" moves, defined by a string of the length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". A single move (character) moves a robot to one of four adjacent cells. Each character is one of the following four: '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"U"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' (up), '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' (down), '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' (left), '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' (right). One move takes one minute."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A cleaning robot must be placed and started in some cell. Then it repeats its pattern of moves till it hits a wall (one of four borders of a house). After hitting a wall it can be placed and used again."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Limak isn't sure if placing a cleaning robot in one cell will be enough. Thus, he is going to start it "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"w·h"},{"kind":"text","text":" times, one time in each cell. Maybe some cells will be cleaned more than once but who cares?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Limak asks you one question. How much time will it take to clean a house? Find and print the number of minutes modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":". It's also possible that a cleaning robot will never stop — then print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without the quotes) instead."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Placing and starting a robot takes no time, however, you must count a move when robot hits a wall. Take a look into samples for further clarification."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"w"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, h, w ≤ 500 000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the length of the pattern, the number of rows and the number of columns, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a string of length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the pattern of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" moves. Each character is one of uppercase letters '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"U"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' or '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one line with the answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If a cleaning robot will never stop, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without the quotes). Otherwise, print the number of minutes it will take to clean a house modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 10 2\nR\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"30\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 4 6\nRUL\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"134\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 1 500000\nRLRL\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample house is a grid with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10"},{"kind":"text","text":" rows and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" columns. Starting a robot anywhere in the second column will result in only one move (thus, one minute of cleaning) in which robot will hit a wall — he tried to go right but there is no third column. Starting a robot anywhere in the first column will result in two moves. The total number of minutes is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10·1 + 10·2 = 30"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample a started robot will try to move \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"RULRULRULR..."}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" For example, for the leftmost cell in the second row robot will make "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":" moves before it stops because of hitting an upper wall."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"611F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/611/problem/F"}